  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Convinced by Kostya's advice, Denis rehearses a romantic marriage proposal for Katya in the kitchen, and Senya and Fedya volunteer to drop rose petals from the balcony during the ceremony. Listen to the rehearsal.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Катя, мы с тобой уже вместе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты наполняешь мою жизнь смыслом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Без тебя я не я.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Без тебя я никто.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И не хочу никем быть.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты мой мир.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты моя жизнь и моя вселенная.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Дорогая моя Катя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты выйдешь за меня?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Как думаете, простит она меня?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Очень круто, точно простит.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "А мы тебе в этом поможем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Обращайте внимание наверх.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Катя, мы с тобой уже вместе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Katya, you and I are together now.' Denis anchors the line on 'Katya', while 'together' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты наполняешь мою жизнь смыслом.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You fill my life with meaning.' The grammar packs 'you' and 'with meaning' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Без тебя я не я.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Without you I am not myself.' Notice how Russian expresses 'without' and 'not' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Без тебя я никто.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Without you I am nobody.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'without' before landing on 'nobody'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И не хочу никем быть.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And I do not want to be anyone else.' The meaning hinges on 'and' working together with 'be' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты мой мир.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You are my world.' Denis addresses the listener with the informal singular 'you' alongside 'world'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты моя жизнь и моя вселенная.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You are my life and my universe.' Denis brings out the contrast between 'you' and 'my' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Дорогая моя Катя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'My dear Katya.' The meaning hinges on 'dear' working together with 'Katya' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты выйдешь за меня?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Will you marry me?' In Russian, the idea of 'you' flows naturally into 'me' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Как думаете, простит она меня?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What do you think, will she forgive me?' Denis anchors the line on 'how', while 'me' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Очень круто, точно простит.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Very cool, she will definitely forgive you.' Notice how Russian expresses 'very' and 'she will forgive' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "А мы тебе в этом поможем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And we will help you with that.' Notice how Russian expresses 'and' and 'will help' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Senya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Обращайте внимание наверх.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Pay attention to the balcony above.' Senya brings out the contrast between 'to turn' and 'attention' in a few short words. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
